@startuml target_session_events_resource_model
title CampusClaw Target Session Events Resource Model

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java c9d858bc8261bf07f5585f545b53495bf2226a56):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java,
' RuntimeEventController.submit and RuntimeEventController.list, lines 39-91.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventStream.java,
' RuntimeEventStream.attach and RuntimeEventStream.detachInternal, lines 89-159.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventQueryService.java,
' RuntimeEventQueryService.list and RuntimeEventQueryService.pageOf, lines 53-99.
' Source evidence (pi-mono 5cd93f688aaab89dbb6dfa4aca535f21796ae185):
' packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts, streamAssistantResponse.
' packages/coding-agent/src/core/agent-session.ts, _handleAgentEvent.
' Observed behavior: the current Java POST owns one execution-scoped SSE stream,
' one RuntimeEventStream permits only one attached subscriber, and GET pagination
' does not bind later pages to a fixed snapshot watermark.
' Target-only design: POST acceptance, live observation, and durable history are
' three separate Session-scoped operations. Execution remains an internal concept.
' Architecture change: a long-lived Session stream can observe multiple executions
' and multiple subscribers; disconnect never cancels or retries a write.
' Design reason: keep write acceptance, best-effort preview, and recovery authority
' separate while preserving pi Agent and Tool lifecycle semantics inside Runtime.
' Supplemental evidence (pi-mono-java a8192e047f4061bd385297d3dc6c4358362d0d49):
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java,
' acceptUserEvent, appendEntry, and appendLocked, lines 55-87 and 208-218.
' campusclaw/src/main/resources/mapper/session/RuntimeSessionMapper.xml,
' lockSessionForUpdate and listCurrentBranch, lines 47-54 and 132-164.
' Observed behavior: transactional sequence allocation and sequence-ordered reads;
' these files are unchanged from c9d858bc8261bf07f5585f545b53495bf2226a56.
' Target-only architecture change: check causal prerequisites at a shared Session
' acceptance boundary before assigning sequence; a DB lock alone cannot infer them.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ActorBorderColor #475569
  ActorFontColor #0F172A
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
  GroupFontColor #334155
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBEA
  BorderColor #A16207
  FontColor #713F12
}

actor "mate-service" as Mate
participant "Runtime Event API\n<<target-only>>" as API
participant "Session Live Hub\n<<target-only>>" as Hub
participant "Event Acceptance / Ordered Append\n<<target-only>>" as Accept
participant "Execution Coordinator\n<<existing, changed>>" as Execution
participant "Event Projector\n<<target-only>>" as Projector
database "Runtime Session Store" as Store
participant "History Query\n<<existing, changed>>" as Query

group Open one Session live stream
  Mate -> API : GET /sessions/{sessionId}/events/stream
  API -> Hub : create connection-scoped subscription
  Hub --> Mate : 200 live-only SSE
end

group Submit one user event independently
  Mate -> API : POST /sessions/{sessionId}/events
  API -> Accept : validated RequestVO and request snapshot
  Accept -> Accept : check prerequisites and determine Session order
  Accept -> Store : short transaction: recheck, allocate sequence, append
  Store --> Accept : committed Entry
  Accept -> Execution : start, interrupt, or resume
  Accept --> API : complete accepted internal event
  API --> Mate : 200 ResultBean JSON
end

loop zero or more internal executions while the live stream stays open
  Execution -> Projector : normalized Agent lifecycle
  alt authoritative event
    Projector -> Accept : append through the same Session ordering boundary
    Accept -> Accept : check prerequisites before sequence allocation
    Accept -> Store : short transaction: recheck, allocate sequence, append
    Store --> Accept : commit succeeds
    Accept --> Projector : committed Entry
    Projector -> Hub : publish completed event
  else transient preview
    Projector -> Hub : publish delta best-effort
  end
  Hub --> Mate : SSE event
end

group Recover from POST uncertainty, SSE gap, or reconnect
  Mate -> API : GET /sessions/{sessionId}/events?filters&page
  API -> Query : fixed filters and opaque page
  Query -> Store : read committed snapshot in internal sequence order
  Store --> Query : ordered authoritative Entries
  Query --> API : fixed-snapshot page
  API --> Mate : 200 ResultBean JSON
end

note over Mate,Hub
Multiple callers may subscribe to the same Session.
Each connection owns a bounded queue and fails independently.
The Hub performs no replay and is never the recovery authority.
end note

note over Accept,Execution
No executionId or runId crosses the HTTP boundary.
The accepted event is durable before success is returned.
Disconnect never cancels execution or retries the POST.
Dependent events cannot precede uncommitted prerequisites.
Independent events use Session acceptance order.
Model calls, tool calls, and prerequisite waits stay outside DB transactions.
end note

note over Store,Query
The first history page captures its watermark and filters.
Every later opaque page remains bound to that snapshot.
The client keeps response array order, never timestamp order.
Public events use eventId; entrySeq remains internal.
end note
@enduml

@startuml target_session_events_classes
title CampusClaw Target Session Events Class Structure

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java c9d858bc8261bf07f5585f545b53495bf2226a56):
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java,
' RuntimeEventController.submit and RuntimeEventController.list, lines 39-91.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventService.java,
' RuntimeEventService.submit and RuntimeEventService.prepareAndSubmit, lines 76-118.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventStream.java,
' RuntimeEventStream.attach, lines 93-100.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/RuntimeSessionControlService.java,
' steer, followUp, abort, and prepareAbort, lines 59-132.
' modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java,
' acceptUserEvent and listCurrentBranch, lines 57-120.
' Observed behavior: current write, query, execution control, and one-subscriber
' streaming responsibilities are split across the cited classes but remain tied
' to one execution-scoped RuntimeEventStream returned by POST.
' Target-only design: all classes and relationships below are target-only unless
' a class is explicitly marked existing-changed.
' Architecture change: event-type strategies replace a central type branch, and
' SessionLiveEventHub replaces RuntimeEventStream as the HTTP observation boundary.
' Design reason: isolate request validation, mutable admission, execution lifetime,
' per-connection backpressure, persistence, and public projection responsibilities.
' Supplemental evidence (pi-mono-java a8192e047f4061bd385297d3dc6c4358362d0d49):
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java,
' onEvent and persistAssistant, lines 105-116 and 238-254.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java,
' appendEntry and appendLocked, lines 76-87 and 208-218.
' Observed behavior: synchronized callbacks and transactional append, unchanged
' from c9d858bc8261bf07f5585f545b53495bf2226a56 for these files.
' Target-only architecture change: all authoritative writers share Session ordering.
' Design reason: prevent a dependent result from winning a race to the DB lock.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
  ArrowColor #64748B
