top to bottom direction

package "Web boundary" {
  class RuntimeEventController <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
  class SubmitSessionEventRequestVO <<request VO, target-only>>
  class AcceptedSessionEventResponseVO <<response VO, target-only>>
}

package "Application" {
  class SessionEventApplicationService <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
  class SessionEventHandlerRegistry <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
  interface SessionEventHandler <<target-only>> {
    +supports(type)
    +accept(snapshot)
  }
  class UserMessageEventHandler <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
  class UserInterruptEventHandler <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
  class UserToolConfirmationEventHandler <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
  class SessionEventAcceptanceSnapshot <<request scope, immutable, target-only>>
  class SessionEventAppender <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
  class SessionEventQueryService <<Spring singleton, existing-changed>>
  class SessionEventSubscriptionService <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
}

package "Runtime core" {
  class RuntimeExecutionCoordinator <<Spring singleton, existing-changed>>
  class RuntimeActiveExecution <<Session execution, existing-changed>>
  class SessionEventProjector <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
}

package "Live observation" {
  interface SessionEventPublisher <<target-only>> {
    +publish(event)
    +publishBestEffort(event)
  }
  class SessionLiveEventHub <<Spring singleton, target-only>>
  class SessionLiveSubscription <<connection scope, target-only>>
}

package "Persistence" {
  interface RuntimeSessionRepository <<existing-changed>>
  class MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository <<Spring singleton, existing-changed>>
  class RuntimeEntryDTO <<persistence DTO, existing-changed>>
}

RuntimeEventController --> SubmitSessionEventRequestVO : validates
RuntimeEventController --> SessionEventApplicationService : submit
RuntimeEventController --> AcceptedSessionEventResponseVO : returns
RuntimeEventController --> SessionEventSubscriptionService : subscribe
SessionEventSubscriptionService --> RuntimeSessionRepository : recheck Session existence
SessionEventSubscriptionService --> SessionLiveEventHub : register and coordinate deletion
RuntimeEventController --> SessionEventQueryService : list fixed snapshot

SessionEventApplicationService *-- SessionEventAcceptanceSnapshot : creates
SessionEventApplicationService --> SessionEventHandlerRegistry : select by type
SessionEventHandlerRegistry o-- "3" SessionEventHandler : immutable handlers
SessionEventHandler <|.. UserMessageEventHandler
SessionEventHandler <|.. UserInterruptEventHandler
SessionEventHandler <|.. UserToolConfirmationEventHandler

UserMessageEventHandler --> SessionEventAppender : accept user event
UserMessageEventHandler --> RuntimeExecutionCoordinator : start
UserInterruptEventHandler --> SessionEventAppender : accept interrupt
UserInterruptEventHandler --> RuntimeExecutionCoordinator : request interrupt
UserToolConfirmationEventHandler --> SessionEventAppender : accept Tool confirmation
UserToolConfirmationEventHandler --> RuntimeExecutionCoordinator : resume Tool flow

RuntimeExecutionCoordinator *-- "0..1 per Session" RuntimeActiveExecution
RuntimeExecutionCoordinator --> SessionEventProjector : normalized lifecycle
SessionEventProjector --> SessionEventAppender : accept authoritative event
SessionEventAppender --> RuntimeSessionRepository : ordered transactional append
SessionEventProjector --> SessionEventPublisher : publish after commit or best-effort
SessionEventPublisher <|.. SessionLiveEventHub
SessionLiveEventHub *-- "0..*" SessionLiveSubscription : bounded queue per connection

SessionEventQueryService --> RuntimeSessionRepository : committed ordered snapshot page
RuntimeSessionRepository <|.. MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository
MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository --> RuntimeEntryDTO : maps records

note right of SessionEventAcceptanceSnapshot
Contains parsed structure, object identity,
locale, and transient credential values.
It never freezes mutable Session state,
pending Tool state, or capacity admission.
end note

note right of AcceptedSessionEventResponseVO
Controller returns a response-specific immutable VO.
DTOs and persistence records never cross the API boundary.
end note

note right of SessionEventAppender
Coordinate by Session, not by HTTP request or producer.
Check source order and committed prerequisites before append.
Recheck mutable state and dependencies in the owning transaction.
Allocate sequence and append atomically; keep the lock until commit.
No model calls, tool calls, or missing-dependency waits in the transaction.
Process-local locking alone is insufficient across service instances.
The class name and scheduling mechanism remain target-only suggestions.
end note

note bottom of SessionLiveSubscription
One slow subscriber cannot block execution or other clients.
Overflow closes only this subscription and requires history repair.
end note
@enduml

@startuml target_session_live_stream_lifecycle
title CampusClaw Session Live Stream - Candidate Lifecycle

' Source evidence (pi-mono-java a8192e047f4061bd385297d3dc6c4358362d0d49):
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java,
' RuntimeEventController.submit and list: POST-scoped SSE; no standalone GET stream.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventStream.java,
' RuntimeEventStream.attach, emit, and emitBestEffort: one subscriber and bounded buffering.
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSseEmitterSubscriber.java,
' onEvent and onHeartbeat: named SSE with optional id; heartbeat comments.
' The cited files are unchanged from c9d858bc8261bf07f5585f545b53495bf2226a56.
' Target-only architecture change: register Session-scoped subscriptions independently
' of execution; data-only frames and connected comments are unconfirmed proposals.
' Design reason: distinguish subscription readiness, durable commit order, preview,
' and transport loss without cancelling or replaying an accepted user request.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #475569
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBorderColor #64748B
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBEA
  BorderColor #A16207
}

actor "mate-service" as Client
participant "Subscription Service\n<<target-only singleton>>" as Service
database "Session Store" as Store
participant "Session Live Hub\n<<target-only singleton>>" as Hub
participant "Subscription Queue + Writer\n<<per connection>>" as Connection
participant "Ordered Event Publisher\n<<target-only>>" as Publisher
participant "History API\n<<target-only>>" as History

Client -> Service : GET /sessions/{sessionId}/events/stream
critical Registration coordinated with Session deletion
  Service -> Store : check Session exists and is not deleted
  Store --> Service : current authoritative state
  Service -> Hub : register one bounded subscription
  Hub -> Connection : create queue and writer
  Hub --> Service : registration ready
end
Service --> Client : 200 text/event-stream, : connected
note over Client,Service
Wait for connected before submitting a separate POST.
This GET never updates credentials of an active execution.
end note

loop new events across multiple executions
  Publisher -> Hub : complete event after commit, in internal order
  Hub -> Connection : enqueue immutable event
  alt queue has capacity
    Connection --> Client : data: JSON with eventId and type
  else complete event cannot be queued
    Hub -> Connection : close only this subscription
    Connection --> Client : transport closes; no business success implied
  end
end

group Idle is not end of subscription
  Publisher -> Hub : committed session.status.idle
  Hub -> Connection : enqueue idle event in order
  Connection --> Client : data: idle event
  Connection --> Client : : ping while waiting for new events
end

group Recover after any transport gap
  Client -> Service : reopen GET stream and wait for connected
  Client -> History : GET /sessions/{sessionId}/events
  History -> Store : query committed fixed snapshot
  Store --> History : ordered authoritative records
  History --> Client : fixed-snapshot page
  Client -> Client : reconcile by eventId; keep history order
end

note over Hub,Connection
Preview may be shed; completed events replace preview.
Network writes never hold the Session DB transaction.
Disconnect does not cancel execution or replay a POST.
No SSE id, Last-Event-ID replay, or public sequence is proposed.
end note
@enduml
